Subject: [PATCH] fix(allwinner): restart the watchdog count on system reset

The system reset sets the watchdog to its shortest timeout, 0.5 s, and
waits. If the watchdog was already running with a longer timeout, its
count is past 0.5 s, so it never fires and the reset fails ("PSCI:
System reset failed") until a power cycle. Restarting the count, with
the key Linux's sunxi_wdt uses, makes the new timeout count from zero.

The TrimUI Smart Pro port (github.com/leow149/trimui-a133-mainline-port,
tf-a patch 0001) found and fixed the same on the A133.
---
 plat/allwinner/common/sunxi_native_pm.c | 6 ++++++
 1 file changed, 6 insertions(+)

diff --git a/plat/allwinner/common/sunxi_native_pm.c b/plat/allwinner/common/sunxi_native_pm.c
index 28abd3c67..bd143b93b 100644
--- a/plat/allwinner/common/sunxi_native_pm.c
+++ b/plat/allwinner/common/sunxi_native_pm.c
@@ -58,6 +58,12 @@ static void __dead2 sunxi_system_reset(void)
 	mmio_write_32(SUNXI_WDOG0_CFG_REG, 1);
 	/* Enable the watchdog with the shortest timeout (0.5 seconds) */
 	mmio_write_32(SUNXI_WDOG0_MODE_REG, (0 << 4) | 1);
+	/*
+	 * Restart the count, as Linux's sunxi_wdt does with WDT_CTRL_RELOAD.
+	 * A watchdog left running with a longer timeout has counted past the
+	 * new one already, and would never reset.
+	 */
+	mmio_write_32(SUNXI_WDOG0_CTRL_REG, (0x0a57 << 1) | 1);
 	/* Wait for twice the watchdog timeout before panicking */
 	mdelay(1000);
 
